# Canonical Lopa example — verification-repair semantics
#
# Lopa is a hard inheritance boundary:
#   1. the target must currently have live written state;
#   2. Lopa consumes that live-written state;
#   3. Lopa clears Anuvrtti context.
#
# A target-less instruction immediately after Lopa is therefore rejected by
# the compiler. The negative case is covered by tests/test_semantic_contract.py.

तन्त्रशास्त्रम् {
    वाचम् लिखति ।   # explicit WRITE establishes target 0x30 + live state
    वाचम् लोपः ।    # explicit LOPA erases 0x30 and clears context
}
